<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albertino Mussato</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1261">1261</a>–<a href="/years/1329">1329</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albertino Mussato was a Paduan statesman, historian and poet, an early figure of Italian humanism. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> tragedy Ecerinis, on the tyranny of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezzelino-iii-da-romano">Ezzelino III da Romano</a>, written in the style of Seneca, warned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> against Cangrande della Scala and earned him the poet's laurel in 1315. He died in exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chioggia">Chioggia</a>.</p></div>
